# Virtual Environment
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Distribution / Packaging
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Logs
*.log
# ...EXCEPT the scheduled-run heartbeat.
#
# `*.log` matched .runs/history.log, so the Heartbeat step's `git add` hit an
# ignored path, exited non-zero, and failed the step — which marked EVERY
# scheduled "Publish case study" run as a failure even when the agent itself
# succeeded (verified: 15 Aug run 31877223677, "Run agent" success, "Heartbeat"
# failure).
#
# The real damage was quieter. That heartbeat exists solely to keep the repo
# active: GitHub disables a scheduled workflow after ~60 days of repository
# INACTIVITY, and workflow runs do not count — only commits do. This agent
# commits to the SITE repo and never to its own, so with the heartbeat unable to
# land, both crons here were on course to switch themselves off around 29
# September 2026, silently and with no failure notification.
!.runs/history.log

# Environment Variables
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

